# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# mount: /devices/bus/board1
# board: yes
# open: /devices
# The namespace, under a real window.
#
# test_mount proves the routing against fakes; what this proves is that
# everything ABOVE the backend seam kept working when a namespace was put
# under it -- a folder window opens on a directory that NOTHING serves,
# lists a store mounted beneath it, and walks into it.
#
# /devices is the case worth having: no filesystem on this host has one,
# so a row appearing in it can only have come from the mount table.
wait 18
note a directory that exists because something is mounted under it
expect-title devices
note holding one row, and that row is synthetic too -- nothing serves
note /devices/bus either, so a listing of /devices can only have got it
note by STATTING a path no store has heard of and being told it is a
note directory because a mount lies below it
expect-rows 1
click-row 0
wait 4
expect-selected-name bus
key Return
wait 12
note and inside it the mount itself, named by the mount rather than by
note whatever the store calls its own root
expect-title bus
expect-rows 1
click-row 0
wait 4
expect-selected-name board1
note and walking into it opens a window on the MOUNTED name, listing what
note the store beneath answers for -- the graft survives a navigation,
note which is the half a unit test of the router cannot reach
key Return
wait 14
expect-title board1
expect-rows-at-least 2
quit
